Linked List:
	It is a implementing class of list interface,Queue interface.
	It is present since jdk 1.2v
	It follows double Linkedlist data structure.
	It stores the object in the form of nodes.
	Because of this LinkedList is good for insertion and deletion operation.
	To perform forward and backward it uses listIterator cursor.
	
Singly LinkedList
Structure: Each mode contains data and a pointer to the next node.
Traversal: Only in one direction(forward)

Doubly LinkedList
Structure: Each node contains data, a pointer to the next node, and a pointer to the previpus node.
Traversal: Can be traversal forward and backward.

Circular Doubly Linked List:
Structure: Combines circular and doubly linked list features.Each node has pointers to both the next node.  
Traversal: Both directions and continous looping.

